§ 310. Prohibited Rituals — The execution of unsanctioned magical rites outside licensed facilities constitutes a Class A Felony under the Accords. Such activities pose unacceptable risks to public safety and environmental integrity. Violators shall be subject to immediate apprehension by Aegis Magi or local law enforcement, followed by summary trial before an Arcane Tribunal for swift adjudication of guilt and punishment.

§ 311. Regulatory Oversight — The Mages' Guild maintains full authority to inspect facilities, review records, and audit practices as deemed necessary to ensure compliance with all provisions herein. Uncooperative entities may be cited for obstruction of justice under applicable statutes. Persistent non-compliance triggers escalation to disciplinary action ranging from fines to revocation of operating privileges entirely.

§ 312. Penalties and Remedies — Convicted violators face a spectrum of sanctions commensurate with the severity of their offenses, including monetary penalties, community service, mandatory retraining, suspension of licenses, or permanent expulsion from the Guild in extreme cases. Restitution payments may be required to cover damages incurred by affected parties. All judgments remain subject to appeal through established channels within thirty days of issuance.

§ 313. Civil Liability — In addition to criminal penalties, individuals and organizations found liable for unsanctioned practices shall indemnify third parties against any losses or injuries resulting from negligent or malicious use thereof. Plaintiffs pursuing civil claims must provide proof of causation linking defendant's actions directly to claimed damages. Statutes of limitations apply uniformly across all causes of action arising hereunder.

see § 200.1 Licensure Required for foundational regulatory mandates; under § 500.1 Field Casting for Value, unauthorized work outside permitted zones incurs additional penalties. This Section incorporates principles laid out in §§ 1.6 Definitions and 1.7 Construction while referencing operational guidelines established under §§ 300.2 Quiet List Procedure and 400.1 Research Permits. Adherence to these strictures ensures responsible advancement of magical knowledge without compromising public welfare or undermining the integrity of the Guild's regulatory framework.


